WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.283
Every system has a noise floor: what remains when there is no signal. In the spectrum it is the carpet the peaks stand on.

2
00:00:07.665 --> 00:00:17.036
The signal-to-noise ratio compares the power of the signal with that of the noise: ten times the logarithm of their ratio. With RMS values it is twenty times the logarithm.

3
00:00:17.736 --> 00:00:25.906
When the noise gets close to the signal, the tone gets lost; as the noise drops it appears clean. Listen to the ratio rise from 0 to 40 dB.

4
00:00:30.957 --> 00:00:39.577
Dynamic range goes from the maximum level before clipping down to the noise floor. In digital audio it is set by the number of bits: about 6 dB per bit.
